ctors of a polynomial."}],"clusters":[{"id":"CL.0094","evidence":"The instructor substitutes a root value into the polynomial."},{"id":"CL.0101","evidence":"The instructor tests each answer choice to find the correct factor."}]},{"start_seconds":498,"end_seconds":616,"summary":"Determine which polynomial function is divisible by a given linear factor.","sub_skills":[{"id":"NLF.4","evidence":"The segment uses the factor theorem to relate roots and factors of a polynomial."}],"clusters":[{"id":"CL.0094","evidence":"The instructor substitutes a root value into the polynomial."},{"id":"CL.0101","evidence":"The instructor tests each answer choice to find the correct factor."}]},{"start_seconds":616,"end_seconds":725,"summary":"Identify factors of a cubic polynomial by testing roots from the choices.","sub_skills":[{"id":"NLF.4","evidence":"The segment uses the factor theorem to relate roots and factors of a polynomial."}],"clusters":[{"id":"CL.0094","evidence":"The instructor substitutes a root value into the polynomial."},{"id":"CL.0101","evidence":"The instructor tests each answer choice to find the correct factor."}]},{"start_seconds":725,"end_seconds":765,"summary":"Use the remainder theorem and a table of values to find a remainder.","sub_skills":[{"id":"NLF.4","evidence":"The segment uses the factor theorem to relate roots and factors of a polynomial."}],"clusters":[{"id":"CL.0072","evidence":"The instructor reads the function value from the table."}]}]$seg$::jsonb),
    ('yTtNjEEoOH8', $seg$[{"start_seconds":0,"end_seconds":17,"summary":"Overview of the steps to find the equation of a line in slope-intercept form.","sub_skills":[],"clusters":[{"id":"CL.0160","evidence":"The instructor explains that m is the slope and b is the y-intercept in the equation y = mx + b."}]},{"start_seconds":17,"end_seconds":49,"summary":"Find the equation of a line given its slope and a point.","sub_skills":[{"id":"LE2.4","evidence":"The segment teaches how to find the equation of a line given its slope and a point."}],"clusters":[{"id":"CL.0047","evidence":"The instructor adds 6 to both sides to isolate b."},{"id":"CL.0094","evidence":"The instructor plugs in the point (-2, -11) and evaluates 3 * -2."},{"id":"CL.0128","evidence":"The instructor writes the partial equation y = 3x + b, plugs in the point, and solves for b."}]},{"start_seconds":49,"end_seconds":95,"summary":"Find the equation of a perpendicular line passing through a given point.","sub_skills":[{"id":"LE2.5","evidence":"The segment teaches how to find the equation of a line perpendicular to a given line."}],"clusters":[{"id":"CL.0047","evidence":"The instructor adds 2 to both sides to isolate b."},{"id":"CL.0094","evidence":"The instructor plugs in the point (14, 3) and evaluates -1/7 * 14."},{"id":"CL.0116","evidence":"The instructor finds the perpendicular slope by taking the opposite reciprocal of 7, which is -1/7."},{"id":"CL.0128","evidence":"The instructor writes the partial equation y = -1/7x + b, plugs in the point, and solves for b."}]},{"start_seconds":95,"end_seconds":145,"summary":"Find the equation of a linear function given two function values, including the y-intercept.","sub_skills":[{"id":"LF.3","evidence":"The segment teaches how to find the equation of a linear function from two function values."}],"clusters":[{"id":"CL.0024","evidence":"The instructor calculates the slope using the slope formula with the two points."},{"id":"CL.0084","evidence":"The instructor iden